  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a 4‑qubit Variational Quantum Classifier (VQC) on highly imbalanced datasets. On the FDA food inspection dataset, VQC achieved macro‑recall 0.87 (similar to QSVM 0.87) while classical stacking reached 0.68; on a credit‑card fraud dataset VQC achieved recall up to 0.99 without SMOTE compared to classical SVM at 0.50. Experiments use small feature‑reduced datasets (4 qubits) on IBM Qiskit simulators and unspecified IBM quantum hardware.",
